# roam-275: ship upstream kNewTabAddsToActiveGroup ENABLED by default — Cmd+T
# (and both new-tab buttons; every route converges on chrome::NewTab) opens the
# new tab inside the active tab's group, at the group's end. When the active
# tab is ungrouped the stock end-of-strip append is unchanged
# (DetermineInsertionIndex untouched — adjacent-to-active placement exists
# upstream only for link opens and "New tab to the right").
#
# WHY: ADR 0002 (roam-241) disabled the fieldtrial testing config in shipped
# and dev builds, which silently turned this behavior OFF (upstream enables it
# for testing via study TabGroupInteractionsDesktop2, arm
# Enabled_NewTabsAddToActiveGroup). This patch is the ADR 0002 follow-through:
# promote the wanted behavior to an explicit compiled default instead of a
# field-trial accident.
#
# OPT-OUT (M149): chrome://flags/#new-tab-adds-to-active-group and
# --disable-features=NewTabAddsToActiveGroup. A user's explicit flags choice
# from an earlier build keeps winning over this default (Local State).
# UPREV CAVEAT: upstream flag-metadata.json sets expiry_milestone 150 for the
# flags entry — at the next repin, reassess the opt-out story (the entry, or
# the feature itself, may be gone; --disable-features works while it exists).
#
# ADR 0003 NOTE: the dedicated upstream suite
# (browser_tab_strip_controller_browsertest.cc) pins this feature explicitly in
# BOTH directions and is immune to the default flip. Any other upstream test
# that groups tabs, opens one via the chrome::NewTab gate and asserts
# end-of-strip placement without pinning would now observe grouped placement —
# tier-2 does not run upstream browser_tests, so triage per ADR 0003's
# applicability test if one surfaces at an uprev; do not blanket-pin.
#
# Coverage: roamux/test/roamux_new_tab_active_group_browsertest.cc — an
# unpinned compiled-default sentinel (RED before this patch, GREEN after) plus
# explicitly pinned enabled/disabled behavioral fixtures (4-tab topology with a
# trailing ungrouped tab so the group-range clamp in TabStripModel::AddTab is
# positionally observable: in-group insert lands BEFORE the trailing tab).
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/ui_features.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/ui_features.cc
index 80d24acaca..2b4d960c76 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/ui_features.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/ui_features.cc
@@ -363,7 +363,7 @@ BASE_FEATURE_PARAM(bool,
 #endif
 
 #if !BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
-BASE_FEATURE(kNewTabAddsToActiveGroup, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+BASE_FEATURE(kNewTabAddsToActiveGroup, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 bool IsNewTabAddsToActiveGroupEnabled() {
   return base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kNewTabAddsToActiveGroup);
